01:26:32.910 --> 01:26:34.100
Tim Ferriss: Okay.

01:26:34.100 --> 01:26:35.460
Andrew Huberman: Minimum, sometimes more.

01:26:35.460 --> 01:26:37.360
Tim Ferriss: Do you take it in one dose or
split doses?

01:26:37.360 --> 01:26:44.850
Andrew Huberman: It ends up being three capsules
with my big meal of the day, which tends to

01:26:44.850 --> 01:26:47.119
be a midday meal.

01:26:47.119 --> 01:26:53.680
And then I do take a tablespoon of the Carlson's
oil and people gasp when I say this, but I

01:26:53.680 --> 01:26:55.560
actually like it on my oatmeal with salt.

01:26:55.560 --> 01:26:56.560
Tim Ferriss: Oh.

01:26:56.560 --> 01:26:57.560
Andrew Huberman: It tastes good.

01:26:57.560 --> 01:26:59.370
Tim Ferriss: When I've spent time —
Andrew Huberman: If you stir it in —

01:26:59.370 --> 01:27:00.739
Tim Ferriss: — in Iceland and Scandinavia
—

01:27:00.739 --> 01:27:01.739
Andrew Huberman: It's delicious.

01:27:01.739 --> 01:27:04.520
Tim Ferriss: — I've had these little shots
of cod liver oil and so on.

01:27:04.520 --> 01:27:05.520
I can do that.

01:27:05.520 --> 01:27:06.520
But on top of the oatmeal?

01:27:06.520 --> 01:27:07.520
Andrew Huberman: No, I'm telling you.

01:27:07.520 --> 01:27:08.850
It's really good.

01:27:08.850 --> 01:27:10.130
And I hate sardines.

01:27:10.130 --> 01:27:11.429
I despise sardines.

01:27:11.429 --> 01:27:13.869
I despise anything smoked flavored.

01:27:13.869 --> 01:27:15.119
I'm really boring.

01:27:15.119 --> 01:27:19.850
And I absolutely loathe anchovies, like fishy
oil smell.

01:27:19.850 --> 01:27:21.230
I don't even really like eating fish.

01:27:21.230 --> 01:27:22.230
Tim Ferriss: Yeah, I can't eat anchovies.

01:27:22.230 --> 01:27:23.230
Still like sardines.

01:27:23.230 --> 01:27:24.230
Andrew Huberman: I like sushi.

01:27:24.230 --> 01:27:25.230
I like sushi.

01:27:25.230 --> 01:27:26.230
That's about it.

01:27:26.230 --> 01:27:27.230
But even there, I'm boring.

