02:00:32.340 --> 02:00:33.500
for the father.

02:00:33.500 --> 02:00:44.440
So, as you go from 30 to 35 to 40, the sperm
age matters, but the increase is still incredibly

02:00:44.440 --> 02:00:45.699
small overall.

02:00:45.699 --> 02:00:50.310
So it's not something you can really point
to and say, "Oh, it's the sperm."

02:00:50.310 --> 02:00:51.940
Or "It's the egg," for that matter.

02:00:51.940 --> 02:00:52.940
Okay.

02:00:52.940 --> 02:00:53.940
Now, dos and don'ts.

02:00:53.940 --> 02:00:57.989
We can now easily look back to the beginning
of our discussion, it's very clear that quality

02:00:57.989 --> 02:01:04.630
sleep on a regular basis, sunlight, keeping
stress in check, healthy relationships, all

02:01:04.630 --> 02:01:07.540
of that is going to support sperm health and
egg health.

02:01:07.540 --> 02:01:08.889
No question about that.

02:01:08.889 --> 02:01:14.020
It's also clear that getting sufficient Omega-3
fatty acids is going to support sperm health

02:01:14.020 --> 02:01:15.020
and egg health.

02:01:15.020 --> 02:01:19.060
I'll just point out that if there were one
supplement that really seems to move the needle

02:01:19.060 --> 02:01:24.790
in terms of egg quality, which is a morphological
but also a meaningful physiological metric

02:01:24.790 --> 02:01:28.869
for sperm quality, which is going to be shape,
motility.

02:01:28.869 --> 02:01:30.050
You don't want dead sperm.

02:01:30.050 --> 02:01:34.100
There are always going to be some in a sample
because of the age of the sperm, et cetera,

02:01:34.100 --> 02:01:35.489
and the way the spermatogenesis cycle go.

02:01:35.489 --> 02:01:38.230
But you want forwardly motile sperm.

02:01:38.230 --> 02:01:41.510
The other ones are called twitchers, so they
just twitch in place.

02:01:41.510 --> 02:01:46.050
They can actually take twitchers and force
them into the egg during IVF, something called

02:01:46.050 --> 02:01:47.050
ICSI.

02:01:47.050 --> 02:01:51.080
But in general, the greater number of forward
motile sperm, I'm swimming them toward you.

02:01:51.080 --> 02:01:52.080
Tim Ferriss: Yeah.

02:01:52.080 --> 02:01:54.271
Andrew Huberman: I'm actually swimming them
at an angle away from Tim.

02:01:54.271 --> 02:01:56.940
But they are —
Tim Ferriss: So forward on our first in-person

02:01:56.940 --> 02:01:57.940
podcast date.

02:01:57.940 --> 02:01:58.940
Andrew Huberman: Exactly.

02:01:58.940 --> 02:02:01.929
Can be greatly increased by supplementation
with L-carnitine.

02:02:01.929 --> 02:02:06.420
So egg health and sperm health greatly enhanced
by L-carnitine.

02:02:06.420 --> 02:02:08.790
Pretty remarkable results there.

02:02:08.790 --> 02:02:12.770
Injectable L-carnitine of about one mil, one
mig per day.

02:02:12.770 --> 02:02:15.429
Now that has to be prescribed by a doctor.

02:02:15.429 --> 02:02:16.969
Tim Ferriss: And that's IM?

02:02:16.969 --> 02:02:17.969
That's intramuscular.

02:02:17.969 --> 02:02:18.969
Yeah.

02:02:18.969 --> 02:02:19.969
Andrew Huberman: Yeah.

02:02:19.969 --> 02:02:20.969
Oral capsules are available over the counter.

02:02:20.969 --> 02:02:23.510
Then you have to get up to four or five grams
per day.

02:02:23.510 --> 02:02:24.510
Tim Ferriss: Oh, wow.

02:02:24.510 --> 02:02:25.510
I was going to ask.

02:02:25.510 --> 02:02:26.510
Yeah.

02:02:26.510 --> 02:02:29.540
Andrew Huberman: And that can increase TMAO
and some other markers that aren't great for

02:02:29.540 --> 02:02:32.250
cardiovascular health because of the way it's
processed by the gut.

02:02:32.250 --> 02:02:38.060
But you can offset that by taking 600 milligrams
of garlic, because of the allicin in garlic.

02:02:38.060 --> 02:02:39.060
Okay.

02:02:39.060 --> 02:02:42.389
Smoking cigarettes, vaping cigarettes —
Tim Ferriss: Really good for sperm.

02:02:42.389 --> 02:02:45.110
Andrew Huberman: Terrible for sperm, terrible
for eggs.

02:02:45.110 --> 02:02:48.960
Smoking cannabis, vaping cannabis, also terrible,
eggs and sperm.

02:02:48.960 --> 02:02:50.050
People don't like to hear that.

02:02:50.050 --> 02:02:53.980
15 percent of women, I can't believe this
statistic, but I've seen it over and over,

02:02:53.980 --> 02:03:00.699
had to check my eyes, but 15 percent ingest
cannabis at some point during pregnancy, 15

02:03:00.699 --> 02:03:01.699
percent.

02:03:01.699 --> 02:03:02.699
Probably not a good idea.

02:03:02.699 --> 02:03:07.060
Now, a lot of people say, "Oh, I smoke weed
every day and got my wife pregnant."

02:03:07.060 --> 02:03:10.260
You never know how healthy your children would've
been.

02:03:10.260 --> 02:03:11.260
You just never know.

02:03:11.260 --> 02:03:12.880
I'm not saying your children are unhealthy,
but you never know.

02:03:12.880 --> 02:03:16.510
Tim Ferriss: There're also going to be, there
will always be edge cases where, "I smoke

02:03:16.510 --> 02:03:20.270
crack every week and never slept for 14 days
