02:03:20.270 --> 02:03:21.270
My kids are great."

02:03:21.270 --> 02:03:22.270
And you're like, "Okay.

02:03:22.270 --> 02:03:25.300
Just because you happen to be the one mutant…"

02:03:25.300 --> 02:03:26.630
Andrew Huberman: Right, yeah.

02:03:26.630 --> 02:03:28.020
If you want to optimize for sperm health.

02:03:28.020 --> 02:03:29.020
Tim Ferriss: If you could thread that needle.

02:03:29.020 --> 02:03:30.020
Andrew Huberman: Exactly.

02:03:30.020 --> 02:03:31.020
Tim Ferriss: Doesn't mean you're a good model.

02:03:31.020 --> 02:03:32.020
Andrew Huberman: Exactly.

02:03:32.020 --> 02:03:33.949
So L-carnitine can really help.

02:03:33.949 --> 02:03:35.989
Avoid smoking anything.

02:03:35.989 --> 02:03:42.079
The issue of tinctures and edibles is a different
subject altogether.

02:03:42.079 --> 02:03:50.770
I think the big wow for me was something,
again, I'm just going to tip my hat to you,

02:03:50.770 --> 02:03:57.159
which is that in 2015, I taught a class at,
I was then a professor at UC San Diego, on

02:03:57.159 --> 02:04:00.389
neural circuits and health and disease, and
I decided to do a lecture on whether or not

02:04:00.389 --> 02:04:06.369
cellphones inhibit sperm health and, or testosterone
level.

02:04:06.369 --> 02:04:08.030
The data were very mixed, frankly.

02:04:08.030 --> 02:04:12.690
There were essentially two good studies in
rats, each of them taking a standard smartphone,

02:04:12.690 --> 02:04:18.190
putting it under a rat's cage, and then looking
at some metrics related to testicular health,

02:04:18.190 --> 02:04:19.370
sperm health, et cetera.

02:04:19.370 --> 02:04:21.570
One showed increases in the testosterone.

02:04:21.570 --> 02:04:22.570
The other showed decreases.

02:04:22.570 --> 02:04:24.660
So it was a disappointing situation.

02:04:24.660 --> 02:04:26.530
So I would present both.

02:04:26.530 --> 02:04:28.590
Now, there is an extensive meta-analysis.

02:04:28.590 --> 02:04:32.780
I can send you this for the show notes if
you like, an extensive meta-analysis of dozens

02:04:32.780 --> 02:04:33.780
of studies.

02:04:33.780 --> 02:04:35.520
Tim Ferriss: I'll add it to the next reprint
of The 4-Hour Body.

02:04:35.520 --> 02:04:41.770
Andrew Huberman: And it very convincingly
shows that keeping the cellphone in one's

02:04:41.770 --> 02:04:44.600
pocket, so this isn't putting it to your head,
this isn't putting it on the desk in front

02:04:44.600 --> 02:04:51.099
of you, but keeping it on and in one's pocket,
and it does not matter if it's on wifi or

02:04:51.099 --> 02:04:53.849
you're using cellular.

02:04:53.849 --> 02:04:59.929
Decreases sperm quality, which means forward
motility, number of healthy sperm per ejaculate,

02:04:59.929 --> 02:05:00.929
et cetera.

02:05:00.929 --> 02:05:07.250
Even ejaculate volume to some extent, N lowers
testosterone overall, which is perhaps not

02:05:07.250 --> 02:05:09.750
surprising, giving the known heat effects
of the phone.

02:05:09.750 --> 02:05:13.040
So even though it doesn't feel hot to the
touch, there are heat effects.

02:05:13.040 --> 02:05:14.040
Sperm don't like heat.

02:05:14.040 --> 02:05:19.199
In fact, the most promising male contraceptive
that's out there that's not a condom, it's

02:05:19.199 --> 02:05:25.320
like a cuff that goes around the vas deferens,
which is the portal from the testes to the

02:05:25.320 --> 02:05:28.980
urethra that allows the ejaculate to leave
the body, that heats that.

02:05:28.980 --> 02:05:33.809
I mean, a sauna, it's not a great form of
contraception because it's not sureproof,

02:05:33.809 --> 02:05:38.940
but it will reduce your total number of motile
sperm by 75 percent or so.

02:05:38.940 --> 02:05:39.940
When I go in the sauna, because I do hope
to —

02:05:39.940 --> 02:05:40.940
Tim Ferriss: 75 percent is a lot.

02:05:40.940 --> 02:05:43.489
Andrew Huberman: — I do hope to conceive
children in some way, so I wear shorts into

02:05:43.489 --> 02:05:49.070
the sauna and I actually put a cold pack at
my groin while I'm in there.

02:05:49.070 --> 02:05:52.910
When the sauna's really hot, it's also, it
makes it a little less unpleasant.

02:05:52.910 --> 02:05:56.860
It's a little painful, but you definitely
don't want to do that on bare skin.

02:05:56.860 --> 02:06:01.719
But I'm chuckling too, but heat is part of
the problem with the cellphone, but it turns

02:06:01.719 --> 02:06:02.719
out, yes.

02:06:02.719 --> 02:06:06.349
And here people are going to think I'm a crazy
person, but they might think that already,

02:06:06.349 --> 02:06:09.030
the EMFs, that business is real.

02:06:09.030 --> 02:06:11.670
Now is it so real that it's giving us gliomas?

02:06:11.670 --> 02:06:12.670
Unclear.

02:06:12.670 --> 02:06:13.670
I'm not going to go there.

02:06:13.670 --> 02:06:18.449
The data aren't in, but it is very clear that
the radiation from phones, the EMFs and the

02:06:18.449 --> 02:06:24.280
heat are combining to reduce sperm quality,
motility and overall testosterone.

02:06:24.280 --> 02:06:25.780
So it's a simple thing.

02:06:25.780 --> 02:06:30.909
Turn off your phone completely, or even better,
just don't put it in your front pocket.

02:06:30.909 --> 02:06:33.150
If you have to put it in a pocket, put it
in your back pocket.

02:06:33.150 --> 02:06:36.699
Even better would be to put it in a shoulder
pocket or a backpack.

02:06:36.699 --> 02:06:43.940
And I'm a weirdo perhaps, but I don't like
keeping the phone to my head too long.

02:06:43.940 --> 02:06:47.219
But that's also because I don't like holding
the phone to my head too long.

02:06:47.219 --> 02:06:51.199
We don't know very much about the effects
of EMFs and heat effects on the different

02:06:51.199 --> 02:06:56.489
tissues of the body, but we now know a lot
about the effects of heat and EMFs on sperm

02:06:56.489 --> 02:07:00.560
quality, and it's not a good picture for the
sperm.

02:07:00.560 --> 02:07:06.159
Tim Ferriss: Where does airplane mode fit
into this equation, if at all?

02:07:06.159 --> 02:07:07.929
In terms of between on and off.

02:07:07.929 --> 02:07:13.559
I mean, does it prevent or mitigate some of
the effects?

02:07:13.559 --> 02:07:15.630
Andrew Huberman: It seems to, it seems to.

02:07:15.630 --> 02:07:18.550
Here's what's really scary about this meta-analysis.

02:07:18.550 --> 02:07:22.659
Their conclusion is that the total amount
of time spent with the phone in the pocket

02:07:22.659 --> 02:07:24.060
is not a strong determinant.

02:07:24.060 --> 02:07:29.360
That it's not all or none, but that the threshold
beyond which you start seeing these damaging

02:07:29.360 --> 02:07:32.290
effects is pretty low.

02:07:32.290 --> 02:07:35.540
So again, here we're talking about a don't,
not a do.

02:07:35.540 --> 02:07:36.760
And so it's pretty straightforward.

02:07:36.760 --> 02:07:41.460
Don't keep the phone in your front pocket
if you're concerned with sperm health and

02:07:41.460 --> 02:07:42.460
testosterone production.

02:07:42.460 --> 02:07:45.140
Now, why is sperm health and testosterone
production so correlated?

02:07:45.140 --> 02:07:48.980
And you say, well, duh, it's because testosterone
and sperm.

02:07:48.980 --> 02:07:52.550
But if you're not interested in conceiving
children, you might not think this is an issue.

02:07:52.550 --> 02:07:57.810
But remember that the two types of cells,
those Leydig cells and the Sertoli cells of

02:07:57.810 --> 02:08:02.290
the testes combine testosterone in the androgen-binding
protein to give rise to sperm.

02:08:02.290 --> 02:08:07.580
So anytime you're seeing a reduction in sperm,
you are definitely seeing that as a reflection

02:08:07.580 --> 02:08:10.940
of reduction in androgen-binding protein,
which means whatever testosterone you have

02:08:10.940 --> 02:08:16.909
around is also not having the effect on that
local organ that it should.

02:08:16.909 --> 02:08:21.130
In other words, the testes and the ovaries
are very interesting organs because they secrete

02:08:21.130 --> 02:08:26.500
hormones into the body to go have effects,
but they also have effects on themselves and

02:08:26.500 --> 02:08:28.070
it's self-amplifying.

02:08:28.070 --> 02:08:30.960
And so this just seems like such a straightforward
one to me.

02:08:30.960 --> 02:08:33.329
And you said this back in, when was The 4-Hour
Body published?

02:08:33.329 --> 02:08:34.530
Tim Ferriss: Came out in 2010.

02:08:34.530 --> 02:08:35.530
Andrew Huberman: Yeah.

02:08:35.530 --> 02:08:38.429
And I remember you and Poliquin and a few
other people saying, "Don't keep the phone

02:08:38.429 --> 02:08:39.429
in your pocket."

02:08:39.429 --> 02:08:43.281
And I remember lecturing to about 400 students
about this, and I would say about half, just

02:08:43.281 --> 02:08:48.280
by my read, about half of the guys in the
class took the phone out of their pocket when

02:08:48.280 --> 02:08:50.420
they heard this.

02:08:50.420 --> 02:08:54.380
I think young people who aren't thinking about
having children at all right now are absolutely

02:08:54.380 --> 02:08:56.020
the ones that should be most concerned.

02:08:56.020 --> 02:09:01.679
Now, it is true, as they told us in high school,
it just takes one sperm, "But it just takes

02:09:01.679 --> 02:09:02.750
one sperm!"

02:09:02.750 --> 02:09:08.820
But in order to get that one sperm to the
egg in vivo, not IVF, but it's called natural

02:09:08.820 --> 02:09:11.960
conception, there's a lot of territory that
needs to be covered.

02:09:11.960 --> 02:09:14.070
There's a lot of chemical environments that
need to be dealt with.

02:09:14.070 --> 02:09:15.710
You want the healthiest sperm.

02:09:15.710 --> 02:09:21.050
Tim Ferriss: So I would say also having gone
through this process with an ex to create

02:09:21.050 --> 02:09:29.829
embryos, even though you can say it only takes
one sperm in IVF as well, you want to stack

02:09:29.829 --> 02:09:34.510
the odds in your favor, which means you need
good morphology, good motility, and you need

02:09:34.510 --> 02:09:37.730
a good count of non-crippled sperm.

02:09:37.730 --> 02:09:38.730
Andrew Huberman: Yeah.

02:09:38.730 --> 02:09:44.389
I mean, sperm analysis, it can be a humbling
thing because no matter what, no one's getting

02:09:44.389 --> 02:09:46.159
100 percent motile, forwardly motile.

02:09:46.159 --> 02:09:50.409
You learn a lot about everyone, males and
females learn a lot about their biology, what

02:09:50.409 --> 02:09:55.290
they're doing well, what they're doing less
well when going down that pathway of IVF,

02:09:55.290 --> 02:09:56.290
I think.

02:09:56.290 --> 02:10:01.850
I think for women, one of the big surprises
is that it doesn't take much ingestion of

02:10:01.850 --> 02:10:09.199
alcohol to diminish egg quality, beyond two
or three drinks per week — per week — you

02:10:09.199 --> 02:10:14.829
really start to see reductions in egg quality
that are probably indirect, through effects

02:10:14.829 --> 02:10:19.909
on diminished sleep and changes in stress
hormones.

02:10:19.909 --> 02:10:23.929
And so again, some people will be more resilient
to this than others.

02:10:23.929 --> 02:10:28.530
People always like to make jokes about how
alcohol facilitates the conception process,

02:10:28.530 --> 02:10:30.099
et cetera.

02:10:30.099 --> 02:10:35.260
I think that in general, if women are having
very regular cycles, whether or not they're

02:10:35.260 --> 02:10:40.369
28 days long or 35 days long, is less important
perhaps than they be fairly regular.

02:10:40.369 --> 02:10:44.619
Women in general tend to know more about their
bodies because they cycle than men.

02:10:44.619 --> 02:10:50.579
But if I could go back in time to my 30s,
I sure would've banked sperm then.

02:10:50.579 --> 02:10:54.889
And I feel good about where I've got my parameters,
but it's really interesting as you learn this,

02:10:54.889 --> 02:11:01.849
you just realize that freezing sperm, freezing
eggs is a great idea, and freezing embryos

02:11:01.849 --> 02:11:08.449
makes sense if you have the appropriate pairing
or situation, and that life gets so much easier

02:11:08.449 --> 02:11:13.849
for those wishing to conceive when you have
healthy embryos frozen in the bank.

02:11:13.849 --> 02:11:18.510
And anyway, for those challenged in that area,
it also becomes this incredibly expensive,

02:11:18.510 --> 02:11:20.389
emotionally and financially expensive battle.

02:11:20.389 --> 02:11:21.389
