02:35:58.029 --> 02:36:03.180
doing, and Nolan in particular, to combine
transcranial magnetic stimulation with psychedelics

02:36:03.180 --> 02:36:04.180
and these sorts of things.

02:36:04.180 --> 02:36:05.180
Tim Ferriss: Oh, that's great.

02:36:05.180 --> 02:36:06.870
I didn't know that about the premium option.

02:36:06.870 --> 02:36:09.760
Andrew Huberman: Yeah, that's really what
the premium channel is designed for.

02:36:09.760 --> 02:36:10.760
Tim Ferriss: Yeah, that's great.

02:36:10.760 --> 02:36:12.090
Andrew Huberman: And this is, again, I'm going
to say this again.

02:36:12.090 --> 02:36:15.450
People are going to think that I'm just here
kissing up to Tim, but I'm doing that over

02:36:15.450 --> 02:36:16.450
text all the time anyway.

02:36:16.450 --> 02:36:22.590
Because this is yet an another example where
you got into science philanthropy early, you

02:36:22.590 --> 02:36:27.090
reached out to your connects, you were very
vocal about what you felt was powerful and

02:36:27.090 --> 02:36:28.800
had worked for you and what you'd been observing.

02:36:28.800 --> 02:36:32.760
And I am absolutely clear, I've said this
on Twitter, I'll say it again.

02:36:32.760 --> 02:36:36.550
When we look back in five years, 10 years,
a hundred years, there's going to be a small

02:36:36.550 --> 02:36:42.290
subset of individuals for whom the transition
